  "implementation": [
    "DoubleMap now owns one actual BaseDoubleMapStorage through private DoubleStorage<A,B>; the contiguous two bucket tables, count, modulus and allocator are canonical. Synthetic Pair, slot/free registries, vector chains and duplicated metadata were removed atomically.",
    "Each insertion allocates a genuine DoubleMapNode with native primary/secondary links, constructs Key2 before Key1, publishes both heads then increments. Borrowed and mixed owned/borrowed Bind/TryBind adapters defer exactly the required clones until after allocation; duplicate validation clones neither key.",
    "Bind lookup hashes each key once and stops at the first duplicate. Public empty lookups skip hash callbacks. Native AreBound hashes both keys before its first search, then deliberately follows primary Next from the secondary head; the oracle proves false for an existing bijection pair when that wrong chain cannot reach it.",
    "Resize stages destination hashes in old primary bucket/chain order, then rewires only actual link fields and commits the native replacement tables. A Rust hash panic before publication retains the old valid two-chain graph. Staging is temporary transition metadata, not another canonical owner.",
    "UnBind1/2 publishes its first unlink before the opposite-key hash callback. If that callback panics, the original link is restored. The opposite chain is searched by pointer identity; a changed inconsistent hash causing a missing partner restores the first chain before a diagnostic panic, avoiding dangling safe-map nodes.",
    "Both links are removed before key/value destruction. Exact typed allocation is released, then count is decremented, matching native DoubleMap order. A Rust destructor panic is captured until cleanup/count update complete. Clear drains primary bucket order, retains old count through callbacks, clears each finished bucket, then zeros secondary heads and finalizes count/table release.",
    "The narrow BaseMapStorage::finish_destroy dependency is reused through BaseDoubleMapStorage::finish_destroy, including the existing raw destroy path. Clear with an allocator always releases tables, even when identity is unchanged; allocator replacement occurs after callbacks.",
    "Concrete DoubleTopology owns Arc<UnsafeCell<BaseDoubleMapStorage>> with a short metadata mutex. Every edit holds the gate; user hash/copy/drop callbacks run outside edits. Observers independently copy actual count/modulus/allocator/table/head identities and never dereference nodes, including native dangling prior-head identities during Clear.",
    "The facade and its readonly ranges preserve proved existing key covariance, Send/Sync/Unpin/unwind bounds. Erased graph pointers plus owned Box<A>/Box<B> markers avoid inheriting the standalone node typed Next2 invariance. Private owner thread impls depend on A/B payload bounds; public raw node/base types gain no blanket thread impls.",
    "Readonly items/values/legacy cursors reuse existing BucketChainPosition over the actual primary table. Their Send/Sync requires both keys Sync but excludes local hasher state. Buckets/SecondBuckets and BasicMapIteratorSource expose actual nodes; native KEY_ONLY generic Key and arrow read Key2.",
    "Assign copies local Key1 then Key2, hashes both locals, allocates and copies node Key2 then Key1, publishes, then drops locals in reverse order. Native target allocator/policies persist. Existing DoubleMap Clone::clone_from retains Assign semantics; Exchange/move swap actual graphs while independent observers remain attached to their original containers.",
    "Native tables and node layouts remain those of the already measured actual classes. New tests inspect real facade nodes, shared allocation offsets, stable retained payload pointers, over-aligned and zero-sized keys, and allocator-before-clone timing. Original public comments and all259doctests are retained."
  ],
